{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates structural awareness of EDIFACT messaging but suffers from critical semantic flattening, missing ~70% of mandatory D96A INVOIC segments, and lacks the qualifier-based distinctions that define EDIFACT semantics. The model conflates distinct business concepts (e.g., all NAD segments, all DTM qualifiers) into generic classes, violating the core principle that EDIFACT semantics are qualifier-driven.",
  "completeness_score": 0.25,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "BGM_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Beginning of Message (BGM) is MANDATORY in D96A INVOIC. Must capture Document Type Code (380=Invoice, 381=Credit Note), Document Number, and Message Function (9=Original). Currently completely absent."
    },
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTM_DocumentDate",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale", "owl_reviewed_length": 4457, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 2}

