{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates a reasonable foundational understanding of EDIFACT structure but suffers from critical incompleteness for D96A EANCOM INVOIC compliance. The model is approximately 35-40% complete, missing ~10-12 mandatory segment types, lacks qualifier-specific distinctions that are semantically critical, and contains several cardinality and data type violations. Most critically, it treats segments as generic classes rather than qualifier-specific semantic entities.",
  "completeness_score": 0.38,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "UNHSegment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "The Message Header (UNH) is MANDATORY in all EDIFACT messages per ISO 9735. It contains the message type identifier (INVOIC), version (D), release (96A), and controlling agency (UN). Without this, the message cannot be identified or routed. This is a foundational segment that must precede all others in the message body."
    },
    {
      "", "owl_reviewed_length": 19078, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 1}

